OVERVIEW: Export files from the archive

USAGE: dicom-archive export --archive <archive> --output <output> [--study-uid <study-uid>] [--series-uid <series-uid>] [--patient-id <patient-id>] [--flatten] [--verbose]

OPTIONS:
  -a, --archive <archive> Path to the archive
  -o, --output <output>   Output directory for exported files
  --study-uid <study-uid> Export by Study Instance UID (0020,000D); one UID or
                          a backslash-separated list (PS3.4 C.2.2.2.2)
  --series-uid <series-uid>
                          Export by Series Instance UID (0020,000E); one UID or
                          a backslash-separated list (PS3.4 C.2.2.2.2)
  --patient-id <patient-id>
                          Export by Patient ID (0010,0020); exact match, no
                          wild cards
  --flatten               Flatten output to <SOP Instance UID>.dcm (no Patient
                          ID / Study / Series subdirectories)
  --verbose               Verbose output
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

